WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.200
Count limpets in twenty random
squares on a rocky shore.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.080
The average comes out at 8 per square.

3
00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.180
Do the same on a second shore.

4
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.330
The average is 8 again.

5
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.560
But on the first shore, almost
every count sits close to 8.

6
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:19.530
On the second, the counts
run from 0 to about 20.

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.090
So what single number
captures that difference?

8
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.610
In this mission, you'll sort
out three different averages:

9
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.560
the mean, the median and the mode.

10
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:33.430
Then you'll see how one extreme
value drags the mean with it,

11
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.710
while the median hardly moves.

12
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.300
Your mission: find the single number
that captures how the two sets of results

13
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:40.910
differ.
